# Milestone: M5
# Covers: D-event-1 determinism rule (spec #3 §10.2): N subscribers on the
#         same event receive emission in registration order; M successive emits
#         maintain that order across all M firings.  Run under all 3 tunable
#         presets × 100 runs each to assert byte-identical output.
#
# defer-to: T59
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture requires:
#     - String literals (not yet lexed/parsed at M5 baseline)
#     - Event.new() constructor (requires globals exposure + T59 stdlib binding)
#     - at (e?) event-subscribe watcher (requires globals access for `e`)
#     - e!(1) event-emit postfix (requires globals access for `e`)
#   All of these require the T59 globals-exposure task.  The tier-2 enter/leave
#   emit hooks (T55), the GC walker amendments (T56), and the ISR drain handler
#   (T57) are tested via unit tests in test_tag_enter_leave.c, test_event_gc.c,
#   and test_isr_event_drain.c respectively.
#
# Activate at T59 by replacing the source below with the uncommented version.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T59):
#   var e = Event.new();
#   var seq = "";
#   at (e?) function (p) { seq = seq + "A" + p };
#   at (e?) function (p) { seq = seq + "B" + p };
#   at (e?) function (p) { seq = seq + "C" + p };
#   e!(1); e!(2); e!(3);
#   echo(seq);
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "A1B1C1A2B2C2A3B3C3"
